 "result_text": "I changed `partition_asymmetry` in `neurom/features/bifurcation.py` so the Uylings variant returns `0.0` when `n + m <= 2`. Before, it raised `NeuroMError`. I haven't run any tests or tried it on a morphology.\n\nThe case you described is exactly the one it now handles. A bifurcation whose two children are both leaves has `n = m = 1`. Both subtrees are the same size, so an asymmetry of 0 is the natural answer. Before, every morphology with such a bifurcation hit the error.\n\nCounting is unchanged. It still counts nodes in each child subtree, not terminal tips as the Uylings paper does. For any bifurcation with larger subtrees, the Uylings formula now gives the same numbers as before.",
